I have been working on getting in instance of irace running on a cluster using SLURM. I implemented a target-evaluator, can return the time used, and can return the job id from target-runner.

However, it seems these 3 things cannot be used in conjunction. Upon running with no target evaluator is the expected error:

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YiWlAb5xWtM/WiZIMIQZo1I/AAAAAAAAAEQ/okfxUl2n7ZMDsefQFJAz3uc1H1eUDnGaQCLcBGAs/s1600/err1.PNG>

When implementing target-evaluator and outputting job id, as the documentation states:

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-apRNNG2Bva0/WiZItFc_6mI/AAAAAAAAAEY/M8voRwqoh6MGUzQrGT2O7ClAwqJ1yl35gCLcBGAs/s1600/err2.PNG>

When implementing target-evaluator and outputting only time, as requested here the output is the same:

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ceu842Jo4eU/WiZJqxJI_eI/AAAAAAAAAEk/ZRVfBjib004MneT316wbj28bBxJXqGV6QCLcBGAs/s1600/err3.PNG>

And when trying them both in conjunction:

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-AmtcsqkpxTg/WiZKOmp7pVI/AAAAAAAAAEs/caYM4FIMI1oeg5gbL_9vONXZKy8ibjUuACLcBGAs/s1600/err4.PNG>

The relevant pieces of code are in race-wrapper.R around line 163:

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ONBnOxZezMw/WiZKsXHoStI/AAAAAAAAAEw/S8h44Vo0fdw_DpJMCP6zcUZfuXodNJ4ywCLcBGAs/s1600/err5.PNG>

And a function regarding qsub, which shouldn't even be called with respect to SLURM, unless it does analagous things with respect to SLURM's sbatch command.
This resides in cluster.R around line 84:

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-agjjjCA-cKM/WiZN9-DjyxI/AAAAAAAAAE8/k3BzTvhF3GkNJvTJSY2vVKymUbETvMkFgCLcBGAs/s1600/err6.PNG>

This is just an issue with these settings, as well. When using max experiments for budgeting, irace begins execution just fine.

