Hi Jeroen,

It seems that in your version of bash, functions like error() need to be defined before being used. Move the code "error(){...}" to the top of the file. Also, put in EXE= just pypy and move the rest to FIXED_PARAMS, otherwise the check for -x EXE cannot work.

If you know python better than bash, you may wish to rewrite target-runner in python directly. There are examples that come with the package.

Cheers,

Manuel.

